Also `arm_rework` — the L2 guard covers rework-on-red-gate-unlatched + rework-on-validation-failed + rework-unresolved-threads (also arm_rework — L4!). Hmm: rework-unresolved-threads is L4 with localAction arm_rework. My guard isVerdictAction(rule) keys on localAction='arm_rework' → it would ALSO defer rework-unresolved-threads (L4) for moved PRs. Is that OK? I5: "moved PR is never parked/reworked/commented in the same tick" — arming rework on a moved PR in the same tick IS what I5 forbids ("never reworked"). The arm itself is a label write on a PR whose threads are unresolved — the threads belong to the OLD head... Deferring it is consistent with I5 and harmless (next tick re-matches). But strictly the ticket lists 4 L2 actions. Keying the guard on localAction catches rework-unresolved-threads too. Hmm — is that a semantic change beyond the ticket? I5 says moved PR is never reworked in the same tick — arming IS the rework arm. I'll keep localAction-keyed guard (simpler + I5-compliant) and document it. Actually wait — let me reconsider: the UT tests (AC7) are per-action keyed on the four L2 actions. The guard keying on localAction covers the four + rework-unresolved-threads. Fine — document in the module comment.

Now, what about `conflict_rework` (L4, localAction) on a moved PR — DIRTY PRs just updated? A DIRTY PR can't be silent-updated (merge fails) → never moved → no interaction. And `reconcile_verdicts` (L0) — comments! I5: never COMMENTED. reconcile posts a comment when stripping... on a moved PR? Reconcile keys on verdict records for the CURRENT head; a moved head → the record's head sha ≠ current → no match (records are head-keyed). Leave it (ticket's guard list doesn't include it).

OK — also `update_branch`'s own park SET path: "a GUEST PR whose current head has RED checks is labeled validation_failed" — could that fire on a head that ANOTHER rule moved this tick? update_branch runs in L1; moves happen in L1 too (itself). Only one update per PR per rule-pass; two update rules (silent-update + park-reset) could BOTH match the same PR? silent-update: mergeState BEHIND; park-reset: labels validation_failed, notLabels ai_validating — disjoint-ish (a BEHIND parked PR matches BOTH: silent-update updates it (moved), then park-reset's query — the ioCache'd list still says BEHIND+parked → matches → update_branch runs AGAIN on the moved PR: uHead resolved via resolveHeadSha — the ticket snapshot... hmm, resolveHeadSha uses ticket.headSha (the cached list's sha) or fetches. The gh-994 head-change reset: parkedHeadVf ≠ current head → unpark fires (label removed) — good (that's the park reset on the move). Then the sticky probes... then refreshHeadSilent AGAIN — the PR is no longer BEHIND → git merge-base ancestor → "already up to date" exit 0 → no real push → freshHeadSha unchanged → not re-recorded (already in set anyway). OK — idempotent, and the second pass's park-unpark is EXACTLY gh-994's intended behavior (head changed → park resets). ✓

One more: since BOTH update rules call recordHeadMovedThisTick → tickMovedPrs deduped by map ✓.

Now — the ordering inside update_branch: my recordHeadMovedThisTick(uHead) call must be inside refreshHeadSilent (after the push). But careful — refreshHeadSilent is ALSO... only called from update_branch's two sites ✓.

Now write the smRuleLayers module. One design question: put it in js/common/ — smAgent requires './common/smRuleLayers.js'. Tests must map it in makeRequire. Also machineSmAgent? machineSmAgent.js is a separate SM (machine merge) — no.

Also — the `test_packRequirePath.js` gate: hoisted require of an existing file → passes.

Let me also double check `resolveWorkflowCap` for the budget initial: workflowBudget.initial = cap. In targeted mode workflowBudget = null → reservation math skipped (helpers guard on workflowBudget) ✓.

Now — IMPORTANT design detail for `ruleBudgetRemaining` when workflowBudget is null: callers guard `workflowBudget &&` first, so the helper can assume non-null. I'll write it defensively anyway.

One more consideration on the effectiveLimit block:

